v1.1.0 engine changes on top of patches 0001-0003 (Hibana d474b74). Applies after 0003; git apply ignores the text
before the first "diff --git" line. compose.yaml sets the v1.1.0 defaults for the opt-in parts.

Opt-in (off unless the environment variable is set):
- engine/think_guard.py (new), engine/spec.py, engine/accept_graphs.py: a repetition guard for thinking, prose and
  code that stops a generation only on a real loop (periodic repeats spanning at least 64 tokens, low n-gram novelty
  over long windows), code-fence and tool-call aware (HIBANA_THINK_GUARD=1, thresholds HIBANA_TG_*). Plus a soft
  </think> bias that ramps up late in the thinking budget, gently and then firmly by 70% of max_tokens, so long
  reasoning closes and still answers (HIBANA_THINK_SOFT_*; 0 bias by default).
- model/flashnext/mtp.py: load a distilled MTP draft head (HIBANA_MTP_WEIGHTS) and its 512 routed experts in 3-bit
  form (HIBANA_MTP_W3_EXPERTS=1, HIBANA_MTP_W3_EXPERTS_PATH). The draft head only proposes tokens; under exact
  acceptance the output distribution stays the target model's.
- model/flashnext/hyper.py, kernels/hyper_mix_cuda.py, kernels/csrc/hyper_mix_{cuda,tc}.cu: fused GB10 (sm_121)
  HyperConnection mix, hoisted FP8 for 1-4 rows and BF16 tensor cores for 5-16 rows (HIBANA_HYPER_MIX_CUDA=16).
- kernels/flashnext_fused.py: route-budget renormalization by the full top-K mass with James-Stein shrinkage
  (HIBANA_ROUTE_PARSEVAL=1, HIBANA_ROUTE_CANDIDATES, HIBANA_ROUTE_BETA).
- model/flashnext/model.py: HIBANA_W3_SKIP_REGEX keeps matching layers out of the 3-bit path.

v1.1.1: engine/spec.py: the host-path </think> bias no longer reads an undefined `batch` (a NameError that stopped
the engine on sampled rounds verified without the device acceptance graph). The bias is added once on every host
path, and skipped when the sampled decision graph already added it.

Always on (no change to outputs):
- kernels/qsa/attention.py: split-K sparse attention for decode and verify rows (1-16 rows, 256+ selected keys).
- kernels/csrc/w3_gemm.cu, kernels/w3.py: a 3-bit GEMM decode kernel with a tunable warps-per-CTA geometry and a
  tuned split for the Flash-Next trunk shape on GB10.
- engine/spec.py: speculative-step results come back through a cached pinned host buffer.
- engine/executor.py: startup warmup also prefills 2,048 and 4,096-token prompts (HIBANA_WARMUP_PREFILL_TOKENS,
  default 4096; 0 turns it off), so the first long prompt after boot pays less kernel JIT time.

